{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 260,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In order for us to see something, it either\nneeds to emit light directly (like the sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4390,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a lightbulb filament or firefly) or else\nhave photons of light bounce off of it and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8310,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into our eyes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9310,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do we see light itself?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11560,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't bounce light off of light (just\nlike you can't bounce slinky waves or ripples"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15750,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the water off of each other - they just\npass right through!), plus, if you \"look\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19510,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at a photon of light in the normal everyday\nway, that means your eye or camera or photodetector"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24190,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will absorb it - and then it's gone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26620,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Destroyed!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27620,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Annihilated!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28620,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like if you want to test how much weight\na bridge can support before it falls down…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32329,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "once you've done your measurement, you have\nthe information you wanted but you no longer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35589,
    "dDurationMs": 1461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have a bridge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37050,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in order to \"see\" light, we need to use\nnon-destructive testing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41390,
    "dDurationMs": 4309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One way of doing that is to make a super dark,\nsuper cold box and cover the inside with a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45699,
    "dDurationMs": 4850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really really shiny mirror - a mirror so excellently\nreflective that photons of light bounce back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50549,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and forth more than a BILLION times before\nbeing absorbed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53469,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In that time, they'll travel a distance equivalent\nto one trip around earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57769,
    "dDurationMs": 4601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This box is also so cold and dark that only\noccasionally will there even be one photon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62370,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inside."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63370,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if there is one, how do we tell without\ndestroying it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66030,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we send an atom through the box, an\natom in a superposition of two different atomic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70720,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "states, just like Schrödinger's cat!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72650,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If there's no photon inside the mirror box,\nthen when the atom comes out the other side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77100,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we'll most likely measure it as being in a\ncertain one of the states - let's call it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80500,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"dead\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81500,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if there is a photon in there, and we\ncarefully send the atom through so it doesn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84810,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually destroy the photon, the atom-photon\ninteractions changes the odds - so now it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89720,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an overwhelming chance that we see that atom\nas \"alive.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93500,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After sending through a few atoms, if they're\nmainly in the \"alive\" state, then we know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97700,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a photon in the box!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99250,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if they're \"dead\": no photon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101500,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's kind of like sending a pinwheel through\na dark chamber, and if it comes out the other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104590,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "side spinning, you know the wind is blowing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106670,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If not?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107670,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No wind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108670,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, once we know there's a photon in\nthere, we can use this cat measurement technique"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112330,
    "dDurationMs": 3730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to measure and manipulate other things about\nthe photon: we can see how long it bounces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116060,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back and forth before it gets absorbed, check\nif it's in a superposition and even force"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120270,
    "dDurationMs": 5690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it into a superposition like Schrödinger's\ncat itself - so, not only can we see light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125960,
    "dDurationMs": 25129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can now use Schrödinger's cat to measure\nSchrödinger's cat: Quantum Catception!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
